Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-06-2001||02:14 PM||||Woops, fergot all about this post conductor.<P>Just leave what ever IAC is in the TB .<BR>I've been mix and matching the TB parts for the past 10+ years, the 84 IAC always worked good on the 85-86 TB's.<P> If it is a different part number, it just might be an updated part.<P> Just be careful removing and installing those IAC motors if you get into that.<BR> The IAC motor housings get brittle with age, and it is easy to snap them off at the treads.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||conductor||12-06-2001||02:58 PM||||Ok, thnx a lot for the info  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Grtx Richard. the Netherlands.||||reg||1
